# Performance — No Unnecessary Delays

This is a payments recovery pipeline. **Even a millisecond of avoidable wait is a bug.**

## Never

- `time.sleep`, busy-wait, or “demo pauses” in request/agent paths
- Sync LLM / Gemini on the hot path when rules already decided the strategy
- Re-run Outcome Evaluator when the path is `delay_and_retry` (Celery owns that later)
- Extra DB round-trips, N+1 queries, or loading unused history
- Blocking the webhook/API thread on long work — queue it (Celery/SQS)

## Always

- Prefer rules → structured state → optional LLM for copy/reasoning only
- LangGraph conditional edges to **skip** nodes that don’t apply (don’t compute then discard)
- Timeouts on every network call; fail fast
- Measure `latency_ms` per agent for Trace — optimize what the Trace shows is slow
- Idempotent short paths: same `payment_id` must not redo expensive work

## When proposing features

Call out **latency cost**. Pick the design that preserves p99 recovery-decision latency.
